\f1\fs22 Tony regained consciousness slowly, his head throbbing in time with the gentle rumble of an engine. He opened his eyes to find himself in the back seat of what appeared to be a meticulously restored 1965 Cadillac Fleetwood, the kind of car that existed only in museums and private collections of the obscenely wealthy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Ah, the Great Teacher awakens," said a familiar voice beside him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony turned, blinking away the fog in his vision, to see the High Elvis sitting next to him in full regalia\'97white jumpsuit, cape, sunglasses, and that unmistakable confident smile. The car was moving through familiar streets.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Did you just kidnap me?" Tony asked, his voice rough.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Recruited," the High Elvis corrected. "With, admittedly, some aggressive persuasion tactics. But desperate times require desperate measures." He gestured out the window. "Look at your kingdom, Great Teacher. See what's become of it."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi Quarter had changed in ways Tony hadn't anticipated. Where once the streets had been unified in their reverence for all things Elvis, now they were sharply divided. On one side, traditional Elvi establishments still operated as before, though with increased security and suspicious glances toward anyone approaching from the opposite side of the street. There, new storefronts had emerged, featuring crosses alongside Elvis iconography and signs promising "Salvation Through Song."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"What the hell happened here?" Tony muttered as the Cadillac glided through the transformed district.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Religious schism," the High Elvis replied grimly. "The government deployed a weaponised gospel virus a few weeks back. Infected about thirty percent of our population. They've been evangelising ever since."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"They did what?" Tony's head snapped up, immediately regretting the sudden movement as pain shot through his skull. "And nobody thought to tell me?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"You've been... unavailable," the High Elvis said diplomatically. "Living in several laps of luxury, I believe you termed it?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The car turned down a familiar street, passing what had been the Memphis Mafia Bar. The famous neon sign now sported a hastily added "& House of Worship" beneath the original name. Armed Elvi guards stood at the entrance, checking patrons for prohibited items.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"That's where they gather," the High Elvis said, pointing. "Pastor Rex Humble holds revival meetings three times a day. Former EV-1732, if you remember him."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony squinted at the building. "The mediocre impersonator? He's running that place now?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Leading a new religious movement, actually. Claims divine inspiration through gospel music." The High Elvis's voice dripped with disdain. "They preach against evolution, against science, against everything we've built."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The car turned again, heading toward downtown. Through the windows, Tony could see more evidence of the divide\'97Elvi wearing makeshift clerical collars sharing unfriendly glances with those sporting evolution-themed buttons on their jumpsuits.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"So what's this festival about?" Tony asked, massaging the back of his head.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Unity through music," the High Elvis replied. "We need to remind our people what we truly believe in. Science, evolution, the power of knowledge over superstition." He looked directly at Tony. "And we need the voice that wrote the Holy Mother's songs to speak for us again."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony stared out the window at his transformed Quarter. "I haven't written anything new in months."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Then you'll have to dig deep, Great Teacher. Because if we lose this battle for hearts and minds, the Elvi might never recover."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Cadillac turned one final corner, revealing a sight that made Tony's breath catch\'97the massive outdoor concert space being constructed for the festival, already drawing crowds of excited Evolution Elvi. Stage techs tested lighting rigs as massive speakers were wheeled into position.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"So," the High Elvis said, "are you with us? Or do we need another pool cue?"\

